tweets.text:
Sixteen pounds of fentanyl, enough to devastate an entire neighborhood, was taken off the streets near Camp Pendleton, CA. During a vehicle stop, a K9 alert led agents to discover seven packages of the deadly narcotic underneath the front seats. The driver is now in DEA custody, facing state drug charges. The passenger, a Mexican national, is in deportation proceedings.

Every seizure of this lethal drug matters. We remain steadfast on the front lines, working each day to keep this poison off our streets.

